<title>UK: ICCO details buffer stock cocoa sales for June.</title>
<headline>ICCO details buffer stock cocoa sales for June.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Cocoa Organization (ICCO) said buffer stock sales for June 1997 will comprise the following:</p>
<p>The following parcels will be sold on descripton:</p>
<p>ORIGINCROP YRPORTTONNAGEQUALITY</p>
<p>Cameroon1981/82Amsterdam 70FF</p>
<p>Cameroon 1987/88Amsterdam100GF</p>
<p>Ivory Coast1980/81Amsterdam 94FF</p>
<p>Ivory Coast1981/82Amsterdam100FF</p>
<p>Ivory Coast1983/84Amsterdam 25GF</p>
<p>Ivory Coast1987/88Amsterdam926GF</p>
<p>Ivory Coast1987/88Amsterdam  1797FF</p>
<p>The following parcels to be sold on description, contract terms subject to rules and regulations for in store cocoa:</p>
<p>ORIGINCROP YRPORTTONNAGEQUALITY</p>
<p>Ghana1986/87Amsterdam 86GF</p>
<p>Ghana1987/88Amsterdam397GF</p>
<p>Ghana1987/88Amsterdam250FF</p>
<p>Malaysia1987/88Amsterdam 49GF</p>
<p>Nigeria1987/88Amsterdam 82GF</p>
<p>The following parcels to be sold as sample drawn and approved by buyers. Arrangements have been made with the relevant warehouse keepers for interested parties to draw their own samples:</p>
<p>ORIGINCROP YRPORTWAREHOUSE KEEPERTONNAGEQUALITY</p>
<p>Ivory Coast1981/82AmsterdamNedveem b.v.172FAQ</p>
<p>Ivory Coast1987/88AmsterdamNedveem b.v.101FAQ</p>
